  "notes": "DIALECT:\nKansai ({関西|かんさい}) dialect, widely used throughout the region including Osaka, Kyoto, and Kobe.\n\nSTANDARD EQUIVALENT:\nそう / そうだ (standard Japanese)\n\nFORMS:\n- せやな - that's right, isn't it\n- せやで - it is, you know\n- せやから - that's why\n- せやけど - but, however\n- せやろ - right? (seeking confirmation)\n- せやせや - yes yes, that's right\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ほんま - really (Kansai)\n- そうや - that's right (variant)\n\nUSAGE:\nVery common in everyday Kansai speech. Often heard in comedy shows and Osaka-based media.",
